<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
CycloneDDS tuning for running many nodes on one machine.

With ROS_LOCALHOST_ONLY=1 multicast is disabled and every participant takes a
fixed index in a small range. MaxAutoParticipantIndex defaults to 9, so the
10th node on the domain fails with:

    Failed to find a free participant index for domain 0
    rmw_create_node: failed to create domain, error Error

race.launch.py starts around ten nodes, so it sits exactly on that limit and a
different node dies each run. Raising the ceiling costs a few more ports.

Use it with:

    export CYCLONEDDS_URI=file://$(ros2 pkg prefix racer_control)/share/racer_control/config/cyclonedds.xml
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <Discovery>
      <MaxAutoParticipantIndex>60</MaxAutoParticipantIndex>
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
